ry good chance  to get back at mozart and deponte in  1786 joseph ii challenged mozart and  salieri to knock their opratic socks off  at a special event a double feature show  in which two one-act operas would be  performed back-to-back the audience  would crown their favorite performance  mozart's piece was the impresario a  musical comedy about the production of a  musical comedy salieri composed a more  ambitious piece in opera set in the  world of opera so it was all rather meta  at the end of the evening salieri was  crowned the winner by the emperor and  the audience so why would he hold a  grudge beyond that in any case salieri  was the most successful and better  enumerated of the two rivals the two  respected each other's music salieri  frequently directed mozart's  compositions and was even happy to hand  over projects to wolfgang when he was  too busy so mozart and daponto really  needn't worry about salieri scheming in  the shadows the first collaboration of  this dream team is in our humble opinion  mozart's finest work the marriage of  figaro the source material was a comedy  by french playwright beaumarshay it had  a revolutionary subtext as it pits the  commoner figaro against the lustful  count of alma viva mozart and deponte  toned down the anti-aristocratic themes  to avoid censorship but their work was  still revolutionary at least in musical  terms and yet the viennese premiere on  may 1 1786 left the audience puzzled the  work was too complex too ahead of its  time but mozart was invited to perform  the opera in prague here the success was  phenomenal the piece remained on stage  for three weeks and mozart was rewarded  with a thousand gilders the prague scene  commissioned another opera from mozart  and dupont the don giovanni before it  was completed the earpod mozart died on  may 28 1787  throughout his life leopold had been a  constant presence in wolfgang's life he  had been his teacher his manager and  even his friend and confidant it was